# Revisions to skip when running `git blame`.
#
# Only whole-tree mechanical rewrites belong here: a commit that changed
# formatting or import order and nothing else. Never add a commit that changed
# behaviour, or blame will hide the change that matters.
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically. For local use, once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Note this repository squash-merges, so the SHA to record is the one that lands
# on main, not the SHA on the pull request branch. Add it in a follow-up commit
# after the merge.

